<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masjed Soleyman</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Masjid-i-Suleiman, Masjed Soleiman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masjed Soleyman is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> on lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> tribes. On 26 May 1908 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-knox-darcy">William Knox D'Arcy</a>'s syndicate struck oil there, the first commercial oil discovery in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>, which led to the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bp">Anglo-Persian Oil Company</a> in 1909. The town grew up as an oil-company settlement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masjed-soleyman.jpg" alt="Masjed Soleyman" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ali Hamed Haghdoust · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masjed_Soleyman_20190304_09.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…foreign companies, such as the Reuter concession of 1872 and the oil concession granted to William Knox D’Arcy in 1901, provoked lasting resentment of foreign influence; the D’Arcy concession led to the discovery of oil at <b>Masjed Soleyman</b> in 1908 and the creation of the Anglo-Persian Oil Company.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The khans negotiated with British companies over the Lynch road and, after oil was found at <b>Masjed Soleyman</b> in 1908, received a share in the oil companies working their lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/bakhtiari-confederation">Bakhtiari confederation</a></li></ul></section>
